          "year": 2020,
          "date_decided": "2020-05-19",
          "holding": "The Eighth Circuit held that the father's and children's substantive and procedural due process claims failed because the officials' reliance on the abuse allegations did not shock the conscience and a petition, emergency hearing and post-deprivation hearing followed the removal within days.",
          "relevance": "The court assesses the adequacy of the investigation that preceded removal under the shocks-the-conscience standard.",
          "quote": "In child removal cases, the meaningful time and manner requirement means that the state must hold a hearing promptly after removal.",
